Content List Type Ordered steps, rankings, sequences <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code> Grouped items (order doesn't matter) <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> Term–description pairs <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> <p>Bad: <pre><code>&lt;!-- Ordered content in an unordered list --&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;First, preheat the oven.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Then, mix the ingredients.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Finally, bake for 25 minutes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</code></pre></p> <p>Good: <pre><code>&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Preheat the oven.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Mix the ingredients.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Bake for 25 minutes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</code></pre></p>

Type Purpose Default Action <code>submit</code> Submits the form Form submission <code>reset</code> Resets the form Form reset <code>button</code> Generic None (JavaScript needed) <p>Important: Inside a <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>, a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> without a <code>type</code> defaults to <code>type="submit"</code>. Outside a form, it defaults to <code>type="button"</code>.</p> <pre><code>&lt;!-- Inside a form: defaults to submit --&gt;
&lt;form&gt;
    &lt;button&gt;Click&lt;/button&gt;  &lt;!-- Submits the form! --&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Best practice: Always specify <code>type</code> explicitly.</p>

